      "side": 1,
      "message": "ADL-RVP is not using Charge Ramping, To disable this, i tried disabling  CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_CHARGE_RAMP_HW\u003dn and CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_CHARGE_RAMP_SW\u003dn \nin the prj.conf but still CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_CHARGE_RAMP_SW is being set to \u0027y\u0027.\nIt looks like, choice \"Charge-ramp method\" is required choice.\n\nFrom internal discussion, I thought this is only required for BC1.2 charging.\nIf its not only for BC1.2 then another way i can think of making this choice optional by adding \"optional\" :\n\t\n\tchoice \"Charge-ramp method\"\n        prompt \"Select the charge-ramp method\"\n        optional\n        help\n          Select the method used for ramping up charging of a battery. It is\n          preferred to use the hardware method if the charger chip can support\n          it. If not, software-controlled charging can be used, with a slight\n          increase in code size.\n          \nWhat your opinion on this? can you suggest any other way of disabling both CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_CHARGE_RAMP_HW and CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_CHARGE_RAMP_SW ?",
